  "components": [
    {
      "name": "Primary Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-primary",
      "description": "Inverted-ink fill for the single primary action in a view.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-primary\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>Add transaction</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-primary{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;background:var(--btn-primary-bg);color:var(--btn-primary-fg);padding:.6rem 1.1rem;border:none;border-radius:var(--radius-md);font-family:var(--font-sans);font-weight:600;font-size:.875rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm);cursor:pointer;transition:background-color var(--transition-fast),box-shadow var(--transition-fast),transform var(--transition-fast)}.ds-btn-primary:hover{background:var(--btn-primary-hover);box-shadow:var(--shadow-md);transform:translateY(-1px)}.ds-btn-primary:active{transform:translateY(0)}.ds-btn-primary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--border-focus);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Secondary Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-secondary",
      "description": "Surface fill on a hairline for every non-primary action, including the sidebar's Record Transaction.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-secondary\">Import statement</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-secondary{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;background:var(--bg-surface);color:var(--text-primary);border:1px solid var(--border-default);padding:.6rem 1.1rem;border-radius:var(--radius-md);font-family:var(--font-sans);font-weight:550;font-size:.875rem;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color var(--transition-fast),border-color var(--transition-fast)}.ds-btn-secondary:hover{background:var(--bg-hover);border-color:var(--border-strong)}.ds-btn-secondary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--border-focus);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ghost Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-ghost",
      "description": "Fill-less tertiary action, used in the sidebar footer and nav bars.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-ghost\">Try the demo</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-ghost{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;background:none;border:none;color:var(--text-secondary);padding:.5rem .75rem;border-radius:var(--radius-md);font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.875rem;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color var(--transition-fast),color var(--transition-fast)}.ds-btn-ghost:hover{background:var(--bg-hover);color:var(--text-primary)}.ds-btn-ghost:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--border-focus);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Segmented Control",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "segmented",
      "description": "Sunken track with a raised pressed segment; switches Net worth and Cash flow.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-seg\" role=\"group\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">Net worth</button><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Cash flow</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-seg{display:inline-flex;gap:2px;padding:3px;border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--bg-subtle);border:1px solid var(--border-subtle);font-family:var(--font-sans)}.ds-seg button{border:none;background:none;padding:.35rem .8rem;border-radius:calc(var(--radius-md) - 3px);font:inherit;font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-muted);cursor:pointer;transition:background-color var(--transition-fast),color var(--transition-fast)}.ds-seg button:hover{color:var(--text-primary)}.ds-seg button[aria-pressed='true']{background:var(--bg-surface-elevated);color:var(--text-primary);box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm)}.ds-seg button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--border-focus);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text Input",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input",
      "description": "Subtle-fill well that lifts to surface with a periwinkle border and wash ring on focus.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-input\" placeholder=\"Search payee or note\" />",
      "css": ".ds-input{width:100%;padding:.625rem .875rem;border-radius:var(--radius-md);border:1px solid var(--border-default);background:var(--bg-subtle);color:var(--text-primary);font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.875rem;outline:none;caret-color:var(--brand-primary);transition:background-color var(--transition-fast),border-color var(--transition-fast),box-shadow var(--transition-fast)}.ds-input::placeholder{color:var(--text-muted)}.ds-input:hover{border-color:var(--border-strong)}.ds-input:focus{background:var(--bg-surface);border-color:var(--brand-primary);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--brand-light)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tag Chip and Money Badges",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "tag-chip",
      "description": "Hairline tag pill plus borderless badges tinted by money meaning.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-chips\"><span class=\"ds-chip\">groceries<button class=\"ds-chip-x\" aria-label=\"Remove\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12\"/></svg></button></span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-in\">income</span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-out\">expense</span><span class=\"ds-badge ds-tr\">transfer</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-chips{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;font-family:var(--font-sans)}.ds-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.35rem;padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:var(--radius-full);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:500;background:var(--bg-subtle);border:1px solid var(--border-default);color:var(--text-primary)}.ds-chip-x{display:flex;border:none;background:none;padding:1px;border-radius:50%;color:var(--text-muted);cursor:pointer}.ds-chip-x:hover{color:var(--color-expense);background:var(--color-expense-subtle)}.ds-badge{display:inline-flex;padding:.2rem .6rem;border-radius:var(--radius-full);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:550;text-transform:capitalize}.ds-in{background:var(--color-income-subtle);color:var(--color-income)}.ds-out{background:var(--color-expense-subtle);color:var(--color-expense)}.ds-tr{background:var(--color-transfer-subtle);color:var(--color-transfer)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "KPI Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "Gradient-lit hairline card with label, tabular figure, delta and a draw-in sparkline.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-card\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-label\">Income · October</span><span class=\"ds-fig\">₹1,20,000</span><span class=\"ds-delta\"><b>↑ 8%</b> vs last month</span><svg class=\"ds-spark\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 36\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"dsg\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"var(--color-income)\" stop-opacity=\".28\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"var(--color-income)\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/></linearGradient></defs><path d=\"M0 28 C40 26 60 18 100 20 S160 8 200 10 S230 6 240 4 L240 36 L0 36 Z\" fill=\"url(#dsg)\"/><path d=\"M0 28 C40 26 60 18 100 20 S160 8 200 10 S230 6 240 4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-income)\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" pathLength=\"1\" class=\"ds-draw\"/></svg></a>",
      "css": ".ds-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.25rem;max-width:280px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--text-primary);background:var(--surface-gradient);border:1px solid var(--border-default);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);padding:1.25rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm);font-family:var(--font-sans);transition:transform var(--transition-normal),box-shadow var(--transition-normal),border-color var(--transition-fast)}.ds-card:hover{border-color:var(--border-strong);transform:translateY(-2px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-md)}.ds-card:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--border-focus);outline-offset:2px}.ds-label{font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-muted)}.ds-fig{font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.2;margin-top:.25rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-delta{font-size:.8125rem;color:var(--text-muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-delta b{color:var(--color-income);font-weight:600}.ds-spark{width:100%;height:36px;margin-top:.5rem;overflow:visible}.ds-draw{stroke-dasharray:1;stroke-dashoffset:1;animation:dsDraw 900ms var(--ease-out-expo) 120ms forwards}@keyframes dsDraw{to{stroke-dashoffset:0}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-draw{animation-duration:1ms;animation-delay:0ms}.ds-card{transition-duration:1ms}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sidebar Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-link-active",
      "description": "Brand lockup with the periwinkle-to-mint mark, and nav rows whose current page is a raised surface with a periwinkle icon.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><div class=\"ds-brand\"><span class=\"ds-mark\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h10\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-name\">Bagstack</span></div><a class=\"ds-link\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"9\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"3\" width=\"7\" height=\"5\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"12\" width=\"7\" height=\"9\" rx=\"1\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"16\" width=\"7\" height=\"5\" rx=\"1\"/></svg>Dashboard</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M7 4v16M17 4v16M3 8h18M3 16h18\"/></svg>Transactions</a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"6\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M3 10h18\"/></svg>Accounts</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;width:240px;padding:1.25rem .875rem;background:var(--bg-app);border-right:1px solid var(--border-default);font-family:var(--font-sans)}.ds-brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;padding:0 .5rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem}.ds-mark{width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:8px;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#0b0c10;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--brand-primary) 0%,var(--brand-mint) 100%);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.18),var(--shadow-sm)}.ds-name{font-weight:650;font-size:1.0625rem;letter-spacing:-.025em;color:var(--text-primary)}.ds-link{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.7rem;padding:.55rem .65rem;border-radius:var(--radius-md);font-size:.875rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-secondary);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color var(--transition-fast),color var(--transition-fast)}.ds-link:hover{background:var(--bg-hover);color:var(--text-primary)}.ds-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--border-focus);outline-offset:2px}.ds-link[aria-current='page']{background:var(--bg-surface-elevated);color:var(--text-primary);font-weight:600;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-default),var(--shadow-sm)}.ds-link[aria-current='page'] svg{color:var(--brand-primary)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Category Standard, Crafted",
    "overview": "Bagstack looks like a modern personal-finance app, deliberately: the category's own grammar (sidebar, KPI row, net-worth trend, spending donut, recent activity) executed at the polish of Copilot Money. The ground is graphite (`#0b0c10` in dark) with a cool-paper light twin (`{colors.cool-paper}`); both themes are first-class and every surface reads from theme variables. Depth comes from hairline borders, gradient-lit neutral cards and soft offset shadows, never from colour glows.\n\nColour is semantic before it is decorative. Ink carries the primary action, periwinkle carries data, selection and focus, and a fixed set of money colours tells you what a number means before you read it: mint in, coral out, sky for transfers, amber for what is due, violet for EMIs. Figures are set in Geist with tabular numerals so columns and KPI values hold still. Density is moderate: a 4-up KPI grid, 16px gaps, 20px card padding.\n\nMotion is spent once. Charts draw their line in on load; cards lift 2px when they are links; everything else is a 150 to 250ms state transition on an expo-out curve, and all of it collapses under `prefers-reduced-motion`. The two rejected looks are confirmed by the user: never a generic indigo SaaS template, never a crypto or trading terminal.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Graphite ground, cool-paper light twin, full light/dark parity through CSS variables.",
      "Inverted-ink primary action, one per view.",
      "Periwinkle reserved for data, selection and focus.",
      "Fixed semantic money colours; a 12-step category palette assigned by rank.",
      "Geist only, tabular figures everywhere money appears.",
      "Hairlines, gradient-lit cards, soft offset shadows, no glows.",
      "One authored motion moment: charts draw in once."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink Primary Rule",
        "body": "The primary action is an inverted-ink fill, never a periwinkle or indigo fill, and there is exactly one per view. Persistent chrome actions (the sidebar's \"Record Transaction\", Import) are secondary.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Periwinkle Reserve Rule",
        "body": "Periwinkle marks data, selection and focus. It is never a button fill and never display or heading text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Money Means Rule",
        "body": "Mint is money in, coral is money out (card debt included), sky is a transfer, amber is due or caution, violet is an EMI. Never use these hues decoratively, and never swap them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rank Rule",
        "body": "Chart categories take `--cat-N` by rank (largest slice is `cat-1`), with \"Other\" on `cat-11`. Colour encodes order, not identity.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every money figure, percentage, axis tick and subtotal uses tabular numerals (`.tabular`, `.kpi-value`, `.kpi-delta`).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Face Rule",
        "body": "Geist throughout. No second display face, no serif, no system-font display.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Glow Rule",
        "body": "Shadows are soft, offset and neutral. No coloured glows, no hard offset shadows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lift-on-Link Rule",
        "body": "Only cards that navigate or act (`card-interactive`) lift, by 2px with the Lift shadow. Static cards only darken their hairline on hover.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** read every colour, shadow and radius from the theme variables in `src/styles/tokens.css` so light and dark stay in parity.",
      "**Do** make the one primary action per view an inverted-ink button (`.btn-primary`); make everything else secondary or ghost.",
      "**Do** keep periwinkle for data series, the current selection and focus.",
      "**Do** colour money by meaning: mint in, coral out (including card debt), sky transfer, amber due, violet EMI.",
      "**Do** assign chart categories from `--cat-1` to `--cat-12` by rank, with \"Other\" on `--cat-11`.",
      "**Do** set every figure in tabular numerals and snap chart axes to round steps.",
      "**Do** use 1px hairlines, 16px card radius, 10px control radius and the soft offset shadow scale.",
      "**Do** lift only interactive cards, by 2px, and let charts draw in exactly once.",
      "**Do** honour `prefers-reduced-motion`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** ship a generic indigo SaaS template: no indigo or periwinkle button fills, no slate-plus-indigo dashboard.",
      "**Don't** drift toward a crypto or trading terminal: no neon, no coloured glows, no ticker density.",
      "**Don't** use periwinkle for headings, display text or button fills.",
      "**Don't** add a second display face or set display type in a system font.",
      "**Don't** add gradients beyond the brand mark, the neutral card surface and chart area fills.",
      "**Don't** hardcode hex colours in new UI; the persisted user palettes in CategoryModal, PayeeTagManagerModal, BankAndCreditAccountModal and TransactionModal store hex by design and are the only sanctioned exception.",
      "**Don't** add new inline-style surfaces; many routes still carry inline styles as debt, and new work should use the shared classes in `src/styles/globals.css`.",
      "**Don't** mirror the category palette in hex; `/reports` still carries a `DONUT_PALETTE` hex copy as debt, and it should read `--cat-N`.",
      "**Don't** add uppercase tracked micro-labels or kickers above titles; label with sentence-case card labels."
    ]
  }
}